---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { projects } from "../../data/projects";

const project = projects.find((project) => project.link === "/work/glp1-guide");
---

<Layout>
  <main>
    <article class="project-page">
      <a class="back-link" href="/">← Back to portfolio</a>

      <header class="project-header">
        <p class="project-label">
          Tri-fold Brochure · Healthcare Industry · Collaborative Project
        </p>
        <h1>{project?.title}</h1>

        <p class="project-intro">
          {project?.description}
        </p>
        <div class="project-resources">
          <a
            class="button"
            href="/files/glp1_trifold.pdf"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            View Final Deliverable
          </a>
          <a
            class="button button-secondary"
            href="/files/glp1-audience-analysis.pdf"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            View Audience Analysis
          </a>
          <a
            class="button button-secondary"
            href="/files/glp-guide-user-education-journey.png"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            View User Journey Map
          </a>
          
        </div>
      </header>

      <section>
        <h2>The Challenge</h2>
        <p>
          Our challenge was to provide trustworthy, accessible information that
          would prepare patients for meaningful discussions with their
          healthcare providers about GLP-1 medication effectiveness, side
          effects, costs, and insurance coverage.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>My Role</h2>
        <p>
          For this project, I served as editor and production specialist. As
          editor, I helped shape the content, keep it within project scope, and
          improve its consistency and readability. As production specialist, I
          created the user education journey map and prepared a presentation
          documenting our group's development process and final deliverable.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Audience</h2>
        <p>
          The brochure was designed for our primary persona, a 57-year-old woman
          who wants to lose 30-50 pounds and is curious about GLP-1 medications.
          She wants to make an informed decision about whether to use a GLP-1
          medication as part of her health journey.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Approach</h2>
        <p>
          To identify our primary audience and content strategy, our team
          conducted a user survey, reviewed industry research, and developed a
          persona, empathy map, and education journey map. We used
          plain-language principles, collaborative writing and editing, and
          iterative reviews to produce the content.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Result</h2>
        <p>
          The final deliverable is practical, accessible, and user-centered. It
          explains how GLP-1 medications work, potential side effects, costs,
          and possible insurance coverage. It also includes a pre-appointment
          checklist and questions readers can ask a healthcare provider when
          considering a GLP-1 medication.
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
